  "message": "I reviewed the diagram and found no architecture defect to correct: every component uses the right typed implementation, and the web app, sign-in, API, function, catalog, model and both test sources are connected, so I left the board unchanged. Still unverified: the application has no acceptance evidence (sign-in, permission denials, update/delete sync, recovery, audit and cleanup); nothing has checked this exact Terraform export against the installed provider schemas; the Bedrock model ID, its access and quotas, and Sydney availability aren't confirmed; region and data country aren't decided; and the real SharePoint/Confluence connectors still have to be built.\n\nHow long should we keep the audit logs, such as 90 days or one year?",
